# --- Frontend (Vite) env. Only `VITE_`-prefixed vars reach the browser bundle. ---

# VITE_API_URL — base URL for the REST API and the SSE stream.
#
# Leave UNSET for local + LAN + tunnel development. It auto-detects:
#   - on localhost      -> http://localhost:4000 (the Nest dev server)
#   - anywhere else      -> same-origin /api, which the Vite dev server proxies
#     to :4000 (see vite.config.ts). This keeps working when the LAN IP or the
#     HTTPS tunnel hostname (trycloudflare / ngrok) changes between runs.
#
# Set it explicitly when there is no Vite proxy in front of the API:
#   - a PRODUCTION build served as static files -> point at the real API origin,
#     e.g. VITE_API_URL=https://api.agendya.app
#   - pointing local dev at a fixed remote backend (staging).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
#
# Hosted builds (GitHub Actions sets this):
#   app-dev.agendya.co  →  VITE_API_URL=https://agendya-dev.up.railway.app
#   app.agendya.co      →  VITE_API_URL=https://api.agendya.co
# Public booking links (copied from the profile form):
#   VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://agendya.co          # prod
#   VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://app-dev.agendya.co  # hosted-dev
# Waitlist (closed beta). Hosted builds get this from GitHub Actions variables.
# VITE_WAITLIST_URL=https://****.***/api/***.php
#
# Build stamp (Vite injects these from git / GITHUB_SHA; you don't set them in .env):
#   VITE_GIT_SHA, VITE_GIT_BRANCH, VITE_BUILT_AT
# Logged on boot as `[Agendya] <branch> @ <sha> · <iso-time>`. Also window.__AGENDYA_BUILD__.
